# add your custom package feeds here
#
# http://www.example.com/path/to/files/packages.adb
#
# GL-MT6000 fork: our own repository (khristophe972-glitch.github.io/
# immortalwrt) comes FIRST and is what matches the running kernel - the CI
# republishes it on every build from the very tree the image was built from.
#
# The upstream packages/luci snapshots are NOT listed (decision 2026-10-30,
# final). An apk index only lists packages that were actually packed, so our
# repository carries what the CI compiled and nothing else - that is the price
# of "apk list -u" coming back empty, which is what we want. Adding the
# upstream indexes back makes the list noisy ("apk list -u" reports any newer
# version, whatever the world says) and buys nothing we still need: the
# packages we require are in the image and republished here.
#
# Consequence to respect: a package the router must be able to install later
# goes into FLOOR_PKGS in build.yml and is built - never into this file.
# Never run a global "apk upgrade" (rule 8). Kernel modules keep coming from
# our targets/ feed via distfeeds.list.
#
# base/ and targets/ come from our repository through the generated
# distfeeds.list, and luci/packages are emitted there commented out because
# build.yml selects them as modules, hence they are listed here explicitly.
https://khristophe972-glitch.github.io/immortalwrt/packages/aarch64_cortex-a53/packages/packages.adb
https://khristophe972-glitch.github.io/immortalwrt/packages/aarch64_cortex-a53/luci/packages.adb
#
# routing/ and telephony/ are NOT published by our CI (404 on gh-pages); they
# stay on upstream on purpose. Nothing installed on the router comes from
# these two, so they do not feed "apk list -u".
https://downloads.immortalwrt.org/snapshots/packages/aarch64_cortex-a53/routing/packages.adb
https://downloads.immortalwrt.org/snapshots/packages/aarch64_cortex-a53/telephony/packages.adb
